1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:00,880
Right now,

2
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,721
you're moving at 1,670

3
00:00:02,721 --> 00:00:04,222
kilometers per hour.

4
00:00:04,242 --> 00:00:05,489
That's how fast the ground

5
00:00:05,489 --> 00:00:06,912
travels at the equator,

6
00:00:06,932 --> 00:00:09,263
as Earth spins once a day.

7
00:00:09,283 --> 00:00:10,206
The farther you are from

8
00:00:10,206 --> 00:00:11,073
the equator,

9
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:12,097
the slower you go.

10
00:00:12,117 --> 00:00:15,755
New York cruises at about 1,270.

11
00:00:15,775 --> 00:00:18,416
London, about 1,040.

12
00:00:18,436 --> 00:00:19,686
At the North Pole,

13
00:00:19,706 --> 00:00:20,675
you're just turning in a

14
00:00:20,675 --> 00:00:21,414
very slow circle.

15
00:00:22,415 --> 00:00:23,752
And that's just the spin.

16
00:00:23,772 --> 00:00:25,116
Earth also races around the

17
00:00:25,116 --> 00:00:26,947
Sun at about 107,000

18
00:00:26,947 --> 00:00:28,302
kilometers per hour,

19
00:00:28,322 --> 00:00:29,487
while the Sun drags us

20
00:00:29,487 --> 00:00:31,646
around the galaxy even faster.

21
00:00:31,666 --> 00:00:34,350
Relax: nobody is stopping those.

22
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:34,819
Today.

23
00:00:36,169 --> 00:00:37,452
So why don't you feel it?

24
00:00:37,472 --> 00:00:38,486
Because everything moves with

25
00:00:38,486 --> 00:00:39,682
you: the ground,

26
00:00:39,702 --> 00:00:40,805
the air, the oceans.

27
00:00:40,825 --> 00:00:42,148
It's like a smooth flight.

28
00:00:42,168 --> 00:00:43,163
You can sip coffee at

29
00:00:43,163 --> 00:00:45,640
900 km/h without spilling a drop.

